Usage: gccli segments search [flags]

Search segments by name or map area.

Flags:
  -h, --help                  Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json                  Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain                 Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header                Print the column names as the first line of
                              --plain output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"          Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING        Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"          Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                              elevations and weights in table and plain output:
                              auto (Garmin profile), metric, statute_us,
                              statute_uk ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version               Print version information.

      --name=TEXT             Text in the segment name.
      --bbox=MINLAT,MINLON,MAXLAT,MAXLON
                              Map area as MINLAT,MINLON,MAXLAT,MAXLON in
                              degrees.
      --activity-type=TYPE    Activity type: cycling or running.
      --classification=KEY    Classification as segments classifications prints
                              it: downhill, hill_climb, hills, other or sprint.
      --surface=KEY           Surface as segments surface-types prints it: dirt,
                              gravel, mixed or paved.
      --min-distance=KM       Minimum distance in kilometers.
      --max-distance=KM       Maximum distance in kilometers.
      --min-grade=PCT         Minimum average grade in percent.
      --max-grade=PCT         Maximum average grade in percent.
  -l, --limit=20              Maximum number of segments to return.
      --offset=0              Number of segments to skip.

